WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.060
Directed by Christopher Nolan, Interstellar
is a fantastic tale of time, space, and love.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.780
But if you got a bit lost in the final act
of the film, we wouldn’t blame you.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:15.040
So let’s do our best to walk through the
bizarre, mind-bending ending of Interstellar.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.400
Life on Earth isn't great in Interstellar.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.500
Massive dust storms are tearing up the planet,
crops are failing, and soon, humanity will

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.480
cease to exist.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.200
Looking for answers, NASA turns to the skies,
hoping for some kind of insight.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.100
"Okay.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.300
Now you need to tell me what your plan is
to save the world."

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.200
As we learn at the beginning of the film,
a group of 12 scientists traveled through

00:00:40.219 --> 00:00:45.579
a mysterious wormhole that appeared near Saturn,
to see if the 12 planets on the other side

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.120
could sustain human life.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.920
A few years later, the Endurance and its crew
including Matthew McConaughey's Cooper and

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.340
Anne Hathaway's Brand are going to visit the
three most promising planets in the hopes

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.300
of colonizing one.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:02.420
When they arrive on Dr. Mann's planet, the
heroic scientist assures them his icy cold

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.880
spot is the perfect place for humans to live.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:12.510
"Our world is cold, stark, but undeniably
beautiful."

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.660
Unfortunately, it's soon all revealed to be
a ruse.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.900
Although each of the original 12 scientists
knew their trip was one-way, Mann admits he

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.090
never fully considered the possibility that
his planet would be uninhabitable, and that

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:25.900
he might die alone.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:31.600
Although he resisted the urge for years, he
eventually falsified his survey data to coax

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.660
another team to travel to his planet, intending
to use the Endurance to escape.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.840
At this point, Mann is so desperate to leave
that he'll do anything, even kill.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.760
Paranoid that the Endurance crew won't go
along with his plan once they learn what he's

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.980
done, Mann attempts to kill Cooper so he can
make his getaway.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.680
Back on Earth, Cooper's now-grown children
find themselves at odds.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:59.880
His daughter, Murph, played by Jessica Chastain,
has realized the surface of our planet has

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.120
become uninhabitable.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:06.040
So naturally, she's trying to persuade her
brother, Tom, to bring his family to the secret

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:10.229
NASA facility where she's been working on
the gravitational equation that would allow

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.960
humanity to escape into space en masse.

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.320
But despite Murph's warnings, Tom refuses
to abandon the farmhouse where they grew up.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.400
After Cooper left them in their grandfather's
care when they were children, never to be

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.560
heard from again, Tom lost all faith in NASA's
ability to help them.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.960
"Dad didn't raise you to be this dumb, Tom."

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.570
"Dad didn't raise me, Grandpa did.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.260
And he's buried out back with Mom and Jesse."

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:39.000
Convinced her brother is making a terrible
mistake, Murph sets fire to Tom's corn fields,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.560
knowing that since Tom relies on his crops
for survival, he'll be forced to drive out

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.400
to try to extinguish the blaze.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.660
That buys Murph enough time to return to the
house and evacuate Tom's wife and son, likely

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.250
in the hopes that once Tom realizes his family
has gone to the NASA facility, he'll have

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.440
no choice but to join them.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.000
Hey, desperate times call for desperate measures.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.940
Without enough fuel to either return to Earth
or travel to the third potentially habitable

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:10.900
planet,, Cooper proposes to use the gravity
of the black hole Gargantua to execute a slingshot

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:16.120
maneuver, which would send the Endurance off
with enough inertia to reach the planet Dr.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.240
Edmunds was sent to assess.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:22.420
However, every time the Endurance crew approaches
the black hole, its gravitational field distorts

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.420
their perception of time due to relativity,
meaning what they experience as only minutes

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:30.620
passes as years for anyone outside Gargantua's
gravity.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:37.220
"Every hour we spend on that planet will be
seven years back on Earth."

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:43.200
By executing Cooper's slingshot maneuver,
he and Brand will experience "time slippage"

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.740
of 51 years.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.900
They both realize this means Cooper will have
to give up hope of ever seeing his children

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.810
back on Earth, as they will likely have died
of old age by the time the Endurance exits

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:54.920
Gargantua's gravity.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.300
Still, Cooper knows that his plan is humanity's
last chance for survival.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.040
Adding even more drama to Cooper's decision
is Mann's earlier speech about the moment

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.840
humans experience before death.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:10.280
According to Mann, as our brains grasp at
survival, we'll experience a vision of the

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.180
thing we most desire to see again.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.340
Mann speculates that Cooper's final image
will be of his children, since they're his

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:17.200
reason for living.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.580
"At the moment of death, your mind is going
to push a little bit harder to survive…

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.260
for them."

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.340
By giving up hope of seeing his children again,
Cooper is prioritizing the future of humanity

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:31.570
over his own motivations for survival.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:37.430
With its depleted fuel supplies, Endurance
must decrease its weight to pull free of Gargantua's

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.240
gravity after completing Cooper's slingshot
maneuver.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:45.300
Before beginning the maneuver, Cooper decides
the shuttle holding TARS will detach and drop

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.180
into the black hole.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.520
In addition to relieving the Endurance of
the shuttle's weight, Cooper hopes that TARS

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.160
can collect the quantum data from inside the
singularity that NASA scientists on Earth

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.200
need to complete the gravitational equation
that will allow humanity to leave.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.900
While odds are slim that TARS will be able
to transmit this data back to Earth, Cooper

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:08.770
is determined to at least try, since it's
his children's last hope of survival.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:13.260
However, Cooper doesn't tell Brand that losing
TARS' shuttle won't account for a big enough

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.160
drop in weight.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.140
In fact, an additional shuttle has to detach
in order for the Endurance to escape.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.900
Cooper decides that he should bite the proverbial
bullet, leaving Brand to continue on to Edmunds'

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.640
planet and restart the human race.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.960
He doesn't tell Brand until the last moment
because he knows she would argue with his

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.970
decision, but even without the possibility
of seeing his children again, Cooper is at

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.480
peace with his probable death.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:41.560
After falling into the black hole, Cooper
continues to record what he's seeing and transmits

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.960
it back to TARS, hoping the additional data
might help the scientists back on Earth.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:51.180
Although he expects to eventually get crushed
by Gargantua's gravity, Cooper is miraculously

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.540
spared once his shuttle is ripped apart.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.340
And that's when things get crazy.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:01.760
After surviving the wild ride, Cooper gets
transported to an infinite, interdimensional

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:05.990
library that allows him to look back into
different moments in his daughter's childhood

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:09.820
bedroom, including the day he left for his
mission on the Endurance.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.120
"If you're leaving, just go."

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.560
"No.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:18.140
No, don't go, you idiot."

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:22.720
TARS determines that they made it through
Gargantua alive because they were protected

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:27.440
by "them," the mysterious beings who constructed
the wormhole in the first place.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.740
Since the beginning of the film, who "they"
are has been a mystery.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:37.220
While NASA realized the wormhole was artificially
constructed by some sort of advanced, intelligent

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:41.620
beings, they didn't have any information about
"them" beyond the assumption that they must

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.540
be benevolent.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:48.720
TARS deduces "they" also must have built this
library to help Cooper understand their five-dimensional

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.280
reality.

00:06:49.729 --> 00:06:54.000
And sure, it's confusing, but it's also nice
to have otherworldly beings on your side.

00:06:55.110 --> 00:07:00.040
Although the library where "they" bring Cooper
seems to go on forever, every part of this

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:05.260
room serves as a window into the exact same
place: his daughter Murph's childhood bedroom.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:09.020
At first, Cooper seems to think he's been
brought to her because of his own desire to

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:14.070
see her again, but TARS helps him understand
"they" have constructed this three-dimensional

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:19.440
reality for Cooper, allowing him to access
all five dimensions in a way he can understand.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.440
And why do they wanna help us, huh?"

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.880
"I don't know, but they've constructed this
three-dimensional space inside of their five-dimensional

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.580
reality to allow you to understand it."

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:33.800
Together, TARS and Cooper figure out that
through the library, Cooper is able to physically

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:38.970
influence different points in space-time by
using gravity to move things, as time and

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:42.960
gravity are the fourth and fifth dimensions
that exist in "their" reality.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.900
But what's the point of all this?

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:49.240
Cooper deduces that he's been brought here
to send a message back through time, using

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.360
gravity, and that Murph has to be the one
to receive it.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.870
Cooper realizes that while he thought "they"
were fixated on him, he's not actually the

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.280
one who's most important to saving humanity
— Murph is.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:06.160
The library exists to ensure that Cooper will
be able to deliver his daughter the information

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:08.420
she needs, right when she needs it.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:15.020
After Cooper finds himself stuck in the library,
he realizes he's supposed to pass along the

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:18.949
quantum data that TARS collected from inside
Gargantua.

00:08:18.949 --> 00:08:24.740
The information the robot gathered from inside
the black hole will help Murph save mankind,

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:30.060
and Cooper is the interdimensional messenger,
selected by the same mysterious forces that

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.870
constructed this library and created the wormhole
near Saturn.

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:35.520
"But something sent you here.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:36.880
They chose you."

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.140
"Well who's they?"

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:43.780
And once Cooper understands his new purpose,
he realizes the creatures who've been assisting

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:46.740
humanity aren't extraterrestrial at all.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.520
"They didn't bring us here at all.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.040
We brought ourselves."

00:08:55.900 --> 00:09:00.800
As it turns out, at some point in the future,
humanity will advance to a place where we

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.500
can navigate through all five dimensions.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:09.100
It's these future humans who used gravity
to create the wormhole that allowed NASA to

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:12.720
send scientists to explore the 12 planets
in the first place.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:18.200
These future humans are also the ones who
protected Cooper from the effects of Gargantua.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.779
Just as Cooper is able to use the library
to influence events that, for him, already

00:09:23.779 --> 00:09:28.350
happened, the humans of the future have been
using their understanding of time and gravity

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:33.730
to ensure their own survival by assisting
Cooper, Murph, NASA, and the other humans

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:34.500
of their past.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.840
After realizing why the library exists and
that "they" want Cooper to give Murph the

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:44.360
quantum data she needs to save the world,
TARS asks how Cooper plans to communicate

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.760
such complex information from another dimension.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:47.960
"Love, TARS, love.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.040
It's just like Brand said.

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.259
My connection with Murph, it's quantifiable.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:53.540
It's the key."

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.210
The robot doesn't understand, but Cooper explains
that he can trust his love for his daughter

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:00.870
to guide him to exactly where he needs to
be.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:05.889
As Brand explained earlier in the film, love
is the only thing that transcends all dimensions,

00:10:05.889 --> 00:10:07.500
including time and space.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:12.160
Cooper decides to code the quantum data into
the second hand of the watch he gave Murph

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:16.399
before he left, assuring TARS that she will
one day return for it.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.339
When TARS asks how Cooper can be sure, he
responds:

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.220
"Because I gave it to her."

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:27.439
He's confident that her love for him will
lead her where she needs to go, just as his

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.980
love led him back to her.

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:34.480
Sure enough, as all this is happening, the
adult Murph has indeed returned to her childhood

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.760
bedroom, drawn by an unseen force.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:41.350
She suddenly understands the "ghost" from
earlier in the film, the entity trying to

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:45.900
contact her with dust patterns on her bedroom
floor, was actually her father.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:51.680
Reminded of her love for him, she finds the
watch, and voila, things are suddenly starting

00:10:51.689 --> 00:10:53.100
to look up for humanity.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.249
With the planet dying, humans have to evacuate
the place fast.

00:10:57.249 --> 00:11:01.489
But to solve the gravitational equation that
allows humanity to escape from the tethers

00:11:01.489 --> 00:11:05.230
of Earth, you need quantum data gathered from
inside a black hole.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.720
"The equation couldn't reconcile relativity
with quantum mechanics.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:09.620
You need more."

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:10.260
"More.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.100
More what?"

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.100
"More data.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.220
You need to see into a black hole."

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:19.320
Thinking that collecting such data is impossible,
Murph believes the people of Earth are doomed,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.140
and that her father has abandoned her.

00:11:21.509 --> 00:11:25.559
However, once she realizes that Cooper was
her childhood "ghost" and that he's given

00:11:25.559 --> 00:11:30.029
her the data she needs through the watch,
she's able to solve the equation, ensuring

00:11:30.029 --> 00:11:31.340
humanity's survival.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:36.480
Once Cooper passes along the quantum data,
the library tesseract begins to collapse,

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.740
having served its purpose.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:42.140
Cooper loses consciousness, and he later wakes
up on a space habitat orbiting Saturn.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:46.820
Just as "they" brought Cooper to a library
and allowed him to communicate with his daughter

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:51.420
and save humanity, "they" also brought him
back back to safety once he was finished with

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:51.920
his mission.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:56.400
Only instead of Earth, he's now on a gigantic
colony floating through space.

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:00.660
Thanks to Murph's calculations and the data
acquired from the black hole, humans were

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:05.240
finally able to leave Earth en masse, and
now they're spread out over several different

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.200
space habitats.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:10.720
And it's all thanks to those mysterious forces,
who helped Cooper in the library and made

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:14.120
sure people would find him once it was time
for the library to close.

00:12:15.249 --> 00:12:19.249
Due to the "time slippage" that Brand warned
about before executing the slingshot maneuver

00:12:19.249 --> 00:12:23.760
around Gargantua, at least 51 years have passed
for the people of Earth.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.640
But it's only been hours for Cooper.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:31.360
By the time he makes it to the space habitat
known as Cooper Station, his daughter Murph,

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:35.120
whom he last saw as a little girl, is an old
woman on the verge of death.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:39.579
On the flip side, Cooper appears to be about
the same age as he was when he left.

00:12:39.579 --> 00:12:44.600
While Cooper is overjoyed to finally be reunited
with his daughter, Murph knows that she won't

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:49.140
live much longer, and tells him that he should
go so that he doesn't have to watch her die.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.380
"No parent should have to watch their own
child die."

00:12:55.600 --> 00:13:00.200
Cooper takes his daughter's advice and steals
a ship, intending to head back through the

00:13:00.209 --> 00:13:02.839
wormhole and join Brand on Edmunds' planet.

00:13:02.839 --> 00:13:08.399
Like Cooper, she would've only recently arrived,
and she'll soon be entering hyper-sleep, keeping

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.340
her the same age until he reaches her.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:15.180
Sadly, Edmunds himself has died at some point
during the decades he spent waiting for NASA

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.560
to send a team to his planet.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:21.800
But as Brand takes off her helmet and breathes
in the air of her new home at his grave site,

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.970
it's evident this is the planet the astronauts
have been searching for, where humanity can

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.300
rebuild and, eventually, thrive again.

